{"id":"d0b34a23-67c1-4087-b88e-90a74404d50e","slug":"memory","name":"Memory","description":"Simulate a 100-cell memory.\n\nThe input is a stream of operations. A READ is the pair `0 addr`; a WRITE is\nthe triple `1 addr value`. Every cell starts at 0. For each READ, output the\ncurrent value of the cell at `addr` — a WRITE produces no output.\n\nFor example, the stream `0 5 1 5 10 1 6 9 0 6 0 5` reads cell 5 (still 0),\nwrites 10 to cell 5 and 9 to cell 6, then reads cells 6 and 5 — so the output\nis `0 9 10`.","extraNotes":"","io":{"input":{"repeat":{"of":"int","label":"op stream","note":"a stream of operations: READ is the pair 0 addr, WRITE is the triple 1 addr value"}},"output":{"repeat":{"of":"int","label":"value","note":"the result of one READ, in operation order"}},"constraints":["The operation stream contains between 2 and 1000 input tokens.","`op` is `0` (READ) or `1` (WRITE)","`0 ≤ addr < 100`","`-1000000 ≤ value ≤ 1000000`"]},"problemSetName":"Semester 1","publicTestData":[{"name":"fresh cell reads zero","in":["0","3"],"out":["0"]},{"name":"write then read","in":["1","7","42","0","7"],"out":["42"]},{"name":"overwrite","in":["1","5","1","1","5","2","0","5","1","5","-5","0","5"],"out":["2","-5"]},{"name":"boundary addresses and values","in":["1","0","-1000000","1","99","1000000","0","0","0","99","0","50"],"out":["-1000000","1000000","0"]},{"name":"write zero, trailing write","in":["0","9","1","9","7","0","9","1","9","0","0","9","1","4","5"],"out":["0","7","0"]},{"name":"reads only","in":["0","0","0","1","0","42","0","98","0","99"],"out":["0","0","0","0","0"]},{"name":"interleaved cells","in":["1","37","120454","1","18","133858","0","37","0","18","0","37","1","16","-339184","1","81","393962","0","16","0","81","0","16","1","61","-610620","1","10","-423270","0","61","0","10","0","61","1","81","399563","1","39","669797","0","81","0","39","0","81","1","63","240094","1","30","568637","0","63","0","30","0","63","1","82","211595","1","19","-300999","0","82","0","19